2 NOTE "Tillisch is a Silesian tribal patricier lineagethat already occurs in the 14th century. A line was 1556 a.m. of Emperor Ferdinand, other lines recorded in 1665 and 1680 in the Bohemian knighthood. The family came to Denmark in th
3 CONC e 17th century Henrik Vilhelm Tillisch (1720-1761) first served as chamber junker, appointed 1746 as county's county officer and shortly before his death as General's Master of The SonFjeld. His son, Colonel, Chamberlain Georg Fre
3 CONC derik Tillisch (1759-1845), whose descendants by royal letter of 22 October 1845, were the first to be sent to the Royal Danish Parliament. On 1July 1872 was recognized as belonging to the Danish nobility, was the father of the co
3 CONC unty of the Faroe Islands, later in Aabenraa County, Chamberlain Christian Ludvig Tillisch (1797-1844), who from 1841 was Christian VIII'svery influential cabinet secretary, to the Council of The GehejmeKonferensråd Frederik Ferdi
3 CONC nand Tillisch (1801-1889), to parish priest of Herlufsholm Parish Paul Christian Tillisch (1805-1876), whose son, Chamberlain George Frederik Tillisch (1835-1917), was first the diocesan husband of the Viborg Diocese,later the cou
3 CONC nty man of Præstø Am andfinally to Maj. Gen. Johan Sigismund Møsting Tillisch (1810-1887)."
3 CONT https://da.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tillisch
