2 CONT
2 CONT ===Note===
2 CONT
2 CONT Missing daughter?
2 CONT
2 CONT * Gift - Sør-Trøndelag fylke, Domkirken i Trondheim, Ministerialbok nr. 601A01 (1679-1728), Forlovererklæringer 1728, sidelenke: [http://www.arkivverket.no/URN:kb_read?idx_kildeid=16323&idx_id=16323&uid=ny&idx_side=-121 Svend Bor?
2 CONC ? og Cornilia Lerche] - 16 sep 1728 - Trondheim
2 CONT
2 CONT Anno 1728 d 16 September have Monsieur Svend Bri? anvist Kongens Bref af dato 18 juni N? at have tilladelse at holde Copulation ?? med Mademoiselle Cornelia Lerche, saa og anvist Copie af afsigten for Capitulets J? Brudts Mads Ler
2 CONC che og Baltzer Heins? saa Indstila?/Intet findes som kand være dem till hinder, hvilket vi som forlovningsmænd siger god for. Bar? Busch Lauridz Brix"
2 CONT
2 CONT They have given a royal permission to be married and this permission has been shown to the witnesses. The witnesses have signed and garanteed that nothing legal should prevent a marriage.
2 CONT
2 CONT I can´t see how their relation is. Annoying that I cannot see the groom´s name. Mads Lerche is a witness, but it was often the brides father or a brother if her father was dead. Christian Corneliussen died in 1720, so if Cornelia 
2 CONC and Mads are related, Mads might be her brother or an uncle. I have tried to find some connection but I did not succeed.
