1 NAME Eugenia Marie /Kielland/
2 GIVN Eugenia Marie
2 SURN Kielland
2 _MARNM Kielland
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE 23 APR 1878
2 PLAC Melby nordre
2 ADDR
3 CITY Skedsmo
3 STAE Akershus
3 CTRY Norge
1 DEAT
2 DATE 7 JUL 1969
2 ADDR
3 CITY Oslo
3 CTRY Norge
1 OCCU Kritiker, litterær konsulent og forfatter. Se Store Norske Leksikon.
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT
2 CONT Eguenia Marie Kielland was born in Skedsmo in Akershus, Norway. She was the daughter of Hjalmar Christian Kielland (1834-1927) and Fredrikke Gleerup Klem (1842-1924). Her father served as mayor of Skedsmo and deputy chairman of Ak
2 CONC ershus amt and Smålenenes amt. She was the granddaughter of author Gustava Kielland.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was educated as a teacher and worked at Olaf Bergs pikeskole 1900-1915 and later at Hegdehaugen skole 1915-1939. She was a literary critic for the newspaper Morgenposten from 1927 to 1963, and was the principal literary consul
2 CONC tant for the publishing house Aschehoug from 1934 to 1960. She was Norwegian editor for the magazine Ord och Bild from 1938 to 1950.
2 CONT
2 CONT Among her books are the poetry collection Vildskud from 1918 and the essay collection Fem essays om moderne norsk litteratur from 1929. Besides essays and articles she also wrote biographical monographs on Nini Roll Anker, Kristia
2 CONC n Elster and Sigurd Christiansen. 
