1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Carl Leander Halvorsen was the youngest and only son of a family of at least 6 children, living in Holmestrand, Norway.   Their father was a custom officer.
2 CONT
2 CONT He went to navy school, after which he gradually worked his way up to the rank of captain.   He worked for Shippig companies for some years until he bought several ships and opened his own shipping company in Shangai, China.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was awarded the medal of bravery from the last Tzar Nikolai II for bringing supplies numerous times from Kamchatka to Vladivostok, through enemy waters during the war between Russia and Japan.   He was also awarded a medal from
2 CONC  China (reason unknown). Maybe for helping out a family in China by giving them a ship. 
