1 OCCU Kammerjunker, Ritmester
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * Odense	Protokol over skifteberegninger og decisioner	1841 - 1862, Folie 40-42 [http://www.ao.salldata.dk/vis1.php?bsid=140472&side=42] - '''''Intet til arvingerne!''''' ___________________________________________
2 CONC _______________________
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Karriere==
2 CONT
2 CONT * Udnævnt Kammerjunker i 1780-erne
2 CONT * Ejer af Christiansdal (Dalum Kloster) ved Odense, 1801 - 1804 [http://www.danskeherregaarde.dk/nutid/christiansdal-fyn]
2 CONT * Ejer af Tirsbæk Gods i Engum Sogn, Hatting Herred, Vejle Amt, 1804 - 1806 [https://da.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tirsb%C3%A6k]
2 CONT * Ejer af gård i Hunderup ved Odense fra 1790-erne - her boede han fra ca. 1811 frem til han lod sig pensionere. _________________________________________________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Livshistorie==
2 CONT
2 CONT Jakob Benzons far havde i 1760’erne købt hovedgården Christiansdal og en del bøndergods i nærheden, og han havde senere oprettet et såkaldt stamhus, som ved hans død i 1801 efter datidens skik overgik til den ældste søn, Jakob. Sø
2 CONC nnen, der i 1780 var udnævnt til kammerjunker, men aldrig opnåede at blive kammerherre, var ikke som faderen en samlernatur, snarere det modsatte, og tre år efter faderens død måtte han i realiteten opgive besiddelserne i Dalum og
2 CONC  overlade stamhuset til en yngre bror.
2 CONT
2 CONT Samtidig knirkede det i kammerjunkerens ægteskab, og en formel skilsmisse kom i stand 1811. Da havde samlivet øjensynlig været afbrudt i flere år, hvor Jakob Benzon flakkede om i udlandet. Da hustruen endelig gik ind på at blive s
2 CONC kilt, svarede kammerjunkeren noget uhøfligt, at det var ham flintrende ligegyldigt, om hun ville skilles eller ej, for han gjorde under alle omstændigheder, som det passede ham! Det var i den grad et brud på datidens normer.
2 CONT
2 CONT Da kammerjunkeren endelig faldt lidt (!) til ro, skete det på en gård i Hunderup, som han havde købt allerede i 1790’erne, men hvor han efter skilsmissen fra sin første kone snart boede sammen med Sophie Catharine Holm, en tidlige
2 CONC re skuespillerinde og operasangerinde fra Det Kongelige Teater. De to blev gift i 1815 og fik sammen seks børn.
2 CONT
2 CONT Noget harmonisk samliv var der vist ikke tale om – ægtefællerne var separeret to gange, men fandt sammen igen – og i Hunderup vakte parret almindelig forargelse og uro, f.eks. når ”actrisen” flygtede rundt i haven skarpt forfulgt 
2 CONC af den ældre ægtemand, eller når uroen på gården var sådan, at omkringboende tilkaldte vægteren. Blå øjne og forvridninger var ikke usædvanlige hos den tidligere skuespillerinde, men det var dog lidt ud over det sædvanlige, da han
2 CONC  en dag brækkede et stoleben af og brugte det i kampen mod hustruen. Ikke underligt, at mødrene i Hunderup brugte kammerjunkeren som ”bussemand”, hvis deres børn ikke ville opføre sig ordentligt.
2 CONT
2 CONT Da kammerjunkeren døde, indrykkede enken en floromvunden dødsannonce i avisen, og kammerjunkeren blev begravet på Assistenskirkegården under en støbejernsplade med et digt, der foregiver at være skrevet af ham selv: ”Besad jeg nog
2 CONC en dyd, regn mig den ej til ære. Jeg havde mange fejl, lad dem forglemte være. Mit støv hensmuldrer her i gravens stille fred fortrøstningsfuldt med håb om Guds barmhjertighed”.
2 CONT
2 CONT En fremsynet kirkegårdsinspektør reddede for mange år siden gravpladen over kammerjunkeren, og den kan nu ses i den lille mindelund ved kirkegårdskontoret. Jakob Benzon var ingen stor forretningsmand. Hans enke bevidnede dog, at h
2 CONC an altid viste velvilje mod sine underordnede og et fransk galanteri imod dem, der var hans ligemænd. Altså en sand adelsmand?
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://odenseleksikon.wordpress.com/personer/jacob-benzon/]
2 CONT
2 CONT https://et.billiongraves.international/grave/Jacob-von-Benzon/9561062
2 CONT
2 CONT Life history
2 CONT
2 CONT In the 1760s, Jakob Benzon's father had bought the main estate of Christiansdal and some nearby farms, and he had later established a so-called family home, which upon his death in 1801, according to the custom of the time, passed
2 CONC  to his eldest son, Jakob. The son, who in 1780 had been appointed chamberlain, but never became chamberlain, was not a collector like his father, quite the opposite, and three years after his father's death he had to give up his 
2 CONC possessions in Dalum and leave the family home to a younger brother.
2 CONT
2 CONT At the same time, the chamberlain's marriage was in trouble, and a formal divorce was obtained in 1811. By then, the couple had apparently been separated for several years, with Jakob Benzon wandering abroad. When the wife finally
2 CONC  agreed to a divorce, the chamberlain replied rather rudely that it was of no concern to him whether she wanted a divorce or not, because he would do whatever he wanted in any case! It was such a breach of the norms of the time.
2 CONT
2 CONT When the chamberlain finally calmed down a bit (!) it happened on a farm in Hunderup, which he had bought already in the 1790s, but where, after his divorce from his first wife, he soon lived with Sophie Catharine Holm, a former a
2 CONC ctress and opera singer from the Royal Theatre. The two were married in 1815 and had six children together.
2 CONT
2 CONT It was certainly not a harmonious life – the couple had separated twice, but got back together – and in Hunderup the couple caused general outrage and unrest, e.g. when the “actress” fled around the garden, hotly pursued by her el
2 CONC derly husband, or when the unrest on the farm was such that the residents called the watchman. Black eyes and contortions were not unusual for the former actress, but it was a bit out of the ordinary when one day he broke a chair 
2 CONC leg and used it in a fight against his wife. No wonder the mothers in Hunderup used the chamberlain as a “busman” if their children would not behave properly.
2 CONT
2 CONT When the chamberlain died, his widow placed a flowery obituary in the newspaper, and the chamberlain was buried in the Assistenskirkegården under a cast-iron slab with a poem purporting to have been written by him: “If I possessed
2 CONC  any virtue, do not credit it to me. I had many faults, let them be forgotten. My dust crumbles here in the quiet peace of the grave, confident in the hope of God’s mercy.”
2 CONT
2 CONT Many years ago, a far-sighted cemetery inspector saved the chamberlain’s gravestone, and it can now be seen in the small memorial grove by the cemetery office. Jakob Benzon was not a great businessman. However, his widow testified
2 CONC  that he always showed goodwill towards his subordinates and a French gallantry towards those who were his equals. So a true nobleman?
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://odenseleksikon.wordpress.com/personer/jacob-benzon/]
2 CONT
2 CONT https://et.billiongraves.international/grave/Jacob-von-Benzon/9561062
