1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Baptized 1. august 1708: "d: 1 Augusti [...] Ditto - Anna Elizabeth - Fad: Capitain Otte Thamsøn - Mod: ___" (Copenhagen, Holmens Church Records, www.sa.dk img. #357)
2 CONT
2 CONT Witnesses: Gehejmeråd Giædel; Admiral von Stüchen; Schoutbynacht Sehested; Mrs. Gehejmerådinde Harboes; Miss Cathrine Vissing [=mother's sister].
2 CONT
2 CONT Went with her father to St. Thomas in the Danish West Indies where he had become governor.
2 CONT
2 CONT Married 21. december 1724 in her home St. Thomas: "Msr. Adrian von Beverhoudt og Frøken Anna Elisabeth Thambsen bleve copulerede i min Svaghed og med min consens af den Reformerte Præst Hr. Grundwald i Brudens Huus." (Den Evangeli
2 CONC ske Menighed på Sankt Thomas og Sankt Jan, opsl. 55)
2 CONT
2 CONT English: "Mr. Adrian von Beverhoudt and Miss Anna Elisabeth Thamsen were married in my weakness and with my consent by the Reformed Priest Mr. Grunwald in the Bride's House."
2 CONT
2 CONT "Beverhout Anna Elisabeth born in Vlissingen[!?] (Thambsen), marr. Adrian v. B. (See: Wissing, testament 19.1.1726) (Royal Orders)"
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Adrian and Anna Elisabeth (Thambson) van Beverhoudt:
2 CONT * 7. i. Lucas van Beverhoudt, b. 25 July 1726, d. 25 July 1726
2 CONT * 8. ii. Johan Jacob Creutzer van Beverhoudt
2 CONT * 9. iii. Pieter Clausen van Beverhoudt
2 CONT
2 CONT According to a Danish biographical lexicon entry on her father, she died on St. Thomas from complications due to childbirth. But this cannot be true, given that she must have been alive at age 48 for her divorce settlement.
2 CONT
2 CONT Chancery Records: 25 Mar 1757 divorce settlement between Adrian v B and Anna Elizabeth v B  - children from both of his marriages mentioned.
